  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A raindrop with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> falls from a cloud at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> above the ground. Assume that the drop is spherical throughout its fall and the force of buoyance may be neglected, then the terminal speed attained by the raindrop is : [Density of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and Density of air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> Coefficient of viscosity of air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
